  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Split the accepted size-L M7-W01-C03 research phase into two bounded size-M units, pure DAG sharing/cycles and finite discontinuity PlotModel. Add 18 durable native planning nodes with exact backlog parity, preserving the original C03 and M7/W01 lifecycle states. Activate S01 for later independent oracles. This is structural research preparation, not a delivered graph or renderer.",
    "value": "The independent C# split gate verifies 2 phases, 4 Q/O/D tasks, 12 subtasks and 541 projected DWF nodes without rewriting existing IDs. It checks split dependencies, explicit Math/AURA separation, no copied AURA scheduler, and unchanged M6/RS109 local-only scientific boundaries. No DAG/PlotModel oracles or advanced package are claimed.",
    "nextAction": "After durable RS110 success, prepare RS111 on M7-W01-C03-S01-T1, now an existing DWF node. Qualify one pure diamond DAG shared-node computation, deterministic cycle refusal and finite node/edge/depth quotas in C#, keeping AURA scheduling and graphical rendering out of Math. Audit RS110 as retry 1 and first-pass NO: one earlier CS0161 refusal occurred before allocation of any attempt.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "Size-L original C03 remains planned and cannot complete before both split research phases and its own aggregate acceptance.",
      "S01 starts as a research phase only; its Q/O/D tasks have not executed a DAG oracle or delivered a runtime API.",
      "S02 requires S01 completion and independent finite 1/x discontinuity and PlotModel budget evidence.",
      "No AURA job scheduler, chart renderer, asynchronous executor, third-party library or public product package is admitted."
    ],
    "achievements": []
  },
